      about: { title: 'About MoliShot', meta: 'Last updated: 2026-05-26 · Version 0.4.0 · macOS 14+', toc: 'Contents', overview: 'Overview', overviewP1: 'MoliShot is a professional screenshot and OCR tool for macOS, built with Swift, AppKit, ScreenCaptureKit, and Vision frameworks. Rather than a simple "system screenshot replacement," it is a complete screen information workflow covering capture, editing, recognition, sharing, and history.', overviewP2: 'The system screenshot tool covers lightweight, instant, zero-learning-curve scenarios; MoliShot handles high-frequency professional use cases, cross-app information organization, and content delivery. Target users include product managers, designers, developers, QA engineers, content creators, educators, and power office users.', features: 'Features', regionCapture: 'Region Capture', regionCaptureDesc: 'Perform region selection on the display under cursor. Supports crosshair selection, window hover highlighting, pixel-level magnifier, and real-time pt/px dimensions. Quick actions: Space to move selection, Shift to lock ratio, Option to scale from center. The overlay is not captured in the final result.', fullscreenCapture: 'Fullscreen Capture', fullscreenCaptureDesc: 'One-click capture of the display under cursor. In multi-display setups, each display can output independently, maintaining actual display pixel dimensions. Supports copy to clipboard, save to file, open in editor, and upload to cloud.', scrollCapture: 'Scroll Capture', scrollCaptureDesc: 'Uses Vision framework VNTranslationalImageRegistrationRequest for frame registration, with manual scrolling and smart stitching. Suitable for long web pages, documents, chat logs, and other scenarios requiring complete capture. Note: stitching may fail when scrolling is too fast, overlap is insufficient, or content jitter is significant.', editor: 'Annotation Editor', editorDesc: 'Editor window opens automatically after capture. Supported annotation types:', editorArrow: 'Arrow — directional annotation', editorRect: 'Rectangle / Ellipse — area highlight', editorLine: 'Line — connector annotation', editorBrush: 'Brush — freehand drawing', editorText: 'Text — double-click to re-edit', editorNumber: 'Auto-numbering — step annotation', editorHighlight: 'Highlight — semi-transparent overlay', editorBlur: 'Blur / Pixelate — privacy masking', editorCrop: 'Crop — adjust capture bounds', editorShortcuts: 'Editor supports ⌘+/⌘- to zoom, ⌘0 to fit window, ⌘1 for actual size. ⌘C to copy, ⌘S to save, ⌘Z to undo last annotation. Status bar shows image dimensions, annotation count, current tool, and zoom level.', ocr: 'OCR Text Recognition', ocrDesc: 'Vision framework-based text recognition with automatic language detection. Result window supports viewing and editing, with recognized text auto-copied to clipboard. Currently plain text output only; text box highlighting and block-by-block copying are not yet supported.', pin: 'Pin Overlay', pinDesc: 'Pin screenshots as floating always-on-top windows. Hover to reveal toolbar. Useful for cross-app reference during design reviews and documentation work.', colorPicker: 'Color Picker', colorPickerDesc: 'Uses system NSColorSampler for a native color picking experience. HEX value auto-copied to clipboard with HUD feedback.', history: 'History', historyDesc: 'Screenshots auto-persisted to Application Support directory. Grid view to browse history. Quickly find and reuse past screenshots.', hotkeys: 'Global Shortcuts', hotkeysDesc: 'Prioritizes CGEventTap for screenshot hotkey interception; automatically falls back to HotKey library when accessibility permission is not granted. Default shortcuts:', export: 'Export & Sharing', exportDesc: 'Three export methods: copy to clipboard, save as PNG file, upload to 0x0.st for shareable links.', preferences: 'Preferences', preferencesDesc: 'Provides shortcut configuration, screen recording/accessibility permission status, history path settings, and more.', techSt